<!-- FAQs Section -->
<section id="faqs" class="faq-section container">
    <div class="section-header">
        <span class="text-primary fw-bold text-uppercase" style="font-size: 0.85rem; letter-spacing: 1px;">Information</span>
        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
        <p>Learn more about how TaskFlow governs and scales project deliverables.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="row justify-content-center">
        <div class="col-lg-8">
            <div class="accordion faq-accordion" id="faqAccordion">
                <!-- FAQ 1 -->
                <div class="accordion-item">
                    <h3 class="accordion-header" id="headingOne">
                        <button class="accordion-button" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseOne" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="collapseOne">
                            How does the codebase-first project onboarding work?
                        </button>
                    </h3>
                    <div id="collapseOne" class="accordion-collapse collapse show" aria-labelledby="headingOne" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                        <div class="accordion-body">
                            When you point TaskFlow to a Git repository, the system clones it locally and runs a semantic syntax scanner. Our integrated Gemini AI service maps modules, structures, and business files to generate a structured backlog of Epics, User Stories, and tasks, alongside test cases.
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <!-- FAQ 2 -->
                <div class="accordion-item">
                    <h3 class="accordion-header" id="headingTwo">
                        <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseTwo" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseTwo">
                            What is RACI and how does it affect workflow transitions?
                        </button>
                    </h3>
                    <div id="collapseTwo" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="headingTwo" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                        <div class="accordion-body">
                            RACI defines roles for tasks: Responsible (who performs the work), Accountable (who approves the work), Consulted (who is consulted), and Informed (who is kept up to date). Stage-gates prevent cards from moving past approval gates (e.g. from Review to Done) unless signed off by the Accountable officer.
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
                <!-- FAQ 3 -->
                <div class="accordion-item">
                    <h3 class="accordion-header" id="headingThree">
                        <button class="accordion-button collapsed" type="button" data-bs-toggle="collapse" data-bs-target="#collapseThree" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="collapseThree">
                            What does "nightly calibration" mean for AI estimations?
                        </button>
                    </h3>
                    <div id="collapseThree" class="accordion-collapse collapse" aria-labelledby="headingThree" data-bs-parent="#faqAccordion">
                        <div class="accordion-body">
                            When AI estimates tasks, it stores the initial forecast. As tasks are completed, developers log actual hours. Every night, TaskFlow runs a background calibration service that computes estimation accuracy ratios and retrains/optimizes prompts to continuously improve Gemini's forecasting.
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

